[
    "LLM compare is a novel method for estimating problem difficulty that operates independently of ground truth information.",
    "LLM compare demonstrates strong robustness to hallucinations.",
    "This approach addresses key limitations of existing difficulty measures.",
    "LLM compare is uniquely suited for scoring out-of-distribution problems.",
    "The LLM compare method consists of two main components.",
    "Large language models perform direct comparisons between pairs of problems to determine which is more difficult.",
    "OpenAI o3 and Gemini 2.5 Pro were used in the study.",
    "BT scores are computed based on pairwise comparisons to generate a continuous difficulty measure for each problem.",
    "The researchers determined an optimal number of matches per problem to achieve reliable convergence in scores while managing computational costs.",
    "For CMCQRD (787 problems): 66 matches per problem.",
    "For Omni-Math (1876 problems): 36 matches per problem.",
    "LLM compare operates without needing performance scores from humans or LLMs.",
    "LLM compare operates without needing reference answers.",
    "LLM compare operates without needing external calibration.",
    "This makes it uniquely suitable for evaluating out-of-distribution problems.",
    "Out-of-distribution problems are problems currently unsolvable by both humans and LLMs.",
    "LLM compare is significantly more robust to hallucinations than other LLM-based difficulty measures.",
    "When simulating hallucinations by introducing noise, LLM compare maintained higher correlation with original difficulty scores compared to both LLM performance and LLM labels.",
    "The resilience to hallucinations stems primarily from LLM compare being a more fine-grained measure that aggregates many individual comparisons.",
    "Occasional errors are overwhelmed by correct judgments.",
    "This robustness pattern held true regardless of which language model was used.",
    "LLM compare scores showed positive correlation with other difficulty measures across multiple datasets.",
    "Other difficulty measures include human labels, human performance, LLM labels, and LLM performance.",
    "The method maintained its effectiveness when implemented with different language models.",
    "The method successfully differentiated between easy and difficult problem tiers in benchmarks.",
    "This innovative approach represents a significant advancement in difficulty estimation.",
    "The approach overcomes the limitations of both time-consuming human annotations and context-dependent LLM-based approaches."
] 

