    "The Dual-Axis RCCL (Representation-Complete Convergent Learning) framework addresses the fundamental challenge of achieving convergent learning across the vast organic chemical space (estimated at 10³⁰–10⁶⁰ possible molecules).",
    "The framework combines two complementary representational axes that together provide comprehensive coverage of chemical structures.",
    "Direct graph enumeration methods like the GDB series (GDB9, GDB11, GDB17) suffer from exponential explosion in the number of structures, making them intrinsically non-convergent.",
    "Sampling-based strategies enable representative sampling but don't directly address whether chemical space admits a finite, representation-complete basis required for convergent learning.",
    "The RCCL framework combines two complementary axes of representation.",
    "GCN0 captures atom-centered valence descriptors based on element type and first-shell coordination, aligning with localized electronic environments from valence bond theory.",
    "GCN1 extends GCN0 to include all 1-hop neighbors of the central atom, achieving structural completeness for localized valence environments.",
    "GCN2 further extends GCN1 by one additional level, enabling representation of higher-order geometric features such as inductive effects, p–π conjugation, and dihedral-angle variations.",
    "NBG0 represents the essential topological units whose properties (valence-bond cooperativity, conjugation, spatial strain) cannot be inferred from local neighborhoods alone.",
    "NBG-Plus extends NBG0 to include isovalent derivatives that can be decomposed along cut edges to yield minimal molecular fragments, aligning with chemical fragmentation paradigms.",
    "The GCN axis captures local valence environments while the NBG axis captures ring/cage topologies that cannot be represented by local neighborhoods alone.",
    "Both axes have relatively limited combinatorial spaces, enabling near-complete coverage of chemical space with finite data.",
    "The FD25 dataset built on this framework shows that model performance converges once a threshold of structural complexity is reached (around LevelGCN2=8, LevelNBG-Plus=3), achieving chemical accuracy (~1 kcal/mol).",
    "Further expansion beyond this threshold yields diminishing returns, confirming the existence of a well-defined convergence point.",
    "The Dual-Axis RCCL approach transforms the traditionally non-convergent challenge of modeling chemical space into a convergent learning problem by establishing a principled basis for dataset construction that ensures both representation completeness and model convergence, even across the vast expanse of organic chemical space."
] 

